Cafe Sales Analysis

1. Structure & Summary Stats

df.info() — checked data types and non-null counts per column
df.describe() — summary statistics (mean, min, max, quartiles) for numeric columns: Quantity, UnitPrice, TotalPrice, Rating

2. Categorical Breakdown

df['Category'].value_counts() — order distribution across Bakery, Beverage, Food, Dessert
df['PaymentMethod'].value_counts() — split across Cash, Card, UPI, Wallet
df['City'].value_counts() — order distribution across Chennai, Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Mumbai, Delhi, Pune

3. Distributions

Histograms plotted for Quantity, UnitPrice, TotalPrice, Rating to check shape/spread of each numeric field

4. Outlier Check

Used the IQR method on TotalPrice: upper_bound = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR
Boxplot to visually confirm outliers
Filtered and listed rows where TotalPrice exceeded the upper bound — these are unusually high-value orders worth a second look

5. Quick Visualizations

Bar chart: Revenue by Category (highest to lowest)
Line chart: Orders over time, grouped by month (OrderDate.dt.to_period('M'))

Purpose: EDA sits between cleaning and final aggregation — it's about understanding the shape, spread, and quirks of the data (not just null-handling) before drawing conclusions in the revenue/customer aggregate queries.
